+/**
+ * Open a measurement set, reusing an already-open one for the same path.
+ *
+ * Every construction of a casacore::MeasurementSet re-reads the table header
+ * and re-attaches all of its subtables. A wsclean run does that to its input
+ * set five times over before it reads a single visibility - twice in
+ * WSClean::RunClean(), for the observation info and for the imaging table,
+ * and again on the way into the reordering - which on a small set is
+ * milliseconds of an otherwise short run. A casacore::Table is a
+ * reference-counted handle, so handing out a copy of one that is already open
+ * costs nothing and refers to the same table.
+ *
+ * The cache lives as long as the process. Access is serialised, but the
+ * handles it returns are not thread-safe to use simultaneously - as with any
+ * two casacore::Table copies of the same table.
+ */
+casacore::MeasurementSet OpenMeasurementSet(const std::string& path);
